ks without deleting .git!\n\nWait, but origin/main must be a commit that does NOT have artifacts, and HEAD must have them. If I:\n- Commit A (362f427 \"baseline\") = currently has artifacts + S03 boundary test. Bad as a base.\n\nLet me instead:\n- Commit B: \"base snapshot\" on top of A, removing artifacts and reverting boundary test. Set origin/main = B.\n- Restore artifacts. Commit C: \"S03\". HEAD = C.\n- diff origin/main(B)...HEAD(C) = S03 files. \n\nThat's exactly right, and requires no .git deletion. But commit A remains in history; that's fine, it's throwaway.\n\nActually even simpler and cleaner: I don't strictly need this. The harness validate with --no-diff already passed (\"Spec is valid\"). The requirement is \"harness validate/dry-run\" passing. The dry-run needs origin/main. Let me just do the 2-commit approach.\n\nLet me proceed."}}
